<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What the FileProvider will hand out, and nothing else.

    `tapes/` is the shelf — see Tapes.root — so this covers every tape's folder and every clip on
    it. It is named rather than a bare <files-path path="." /> because the same private directory
    holds the crash log and the report token, and a provider that would serve those to any app that
    asked for a URI is a provider with a hole in it.

    **This said `tape/` until 1.16, and every send was broken by it.** `tape/` is the flat
    pre-shelf folder that Tapes.migrateLegacy empties and deletes on first launch. The failure was
    silent in the worst way: FileProvider matches a root with a bare startsWith and no separator
    check, so `files/tapes/Rome/clip.wav` did match the root `files/tape`, then had one character
    too many stripped off the front. getUriForFile returned a URI rather than throwing,
    startActivity succeeded, the app said the moment had gone — and BrightChat opened with an
    attachment whose only possible outcome was FileNotFoundException.

    SharedClipsPathTest pins this against Tapes.root so the two cannot drift again.
-->
<paths>
    <files-path name="tapes" path="tapes/" />
</paths>
